#!/usr/bin/python3
"""hearth-discord: Discord on Hearth OS (docs/DISCORD.md). Since 1.6 Discord is how Hearth does friends (Hearth Friends
on Matrix is archived, docs/archive/FRIENDS.md).

Hearth only starts, shows, places and hides Discord's own window. It never reads, scripts or injects into that window
or its storage, never touches a Discord token, password or cookie, and never reads or sends messages or the friends
list. "Playing <game>", Ask to join / Join and Play together go through the Discord app's own local IPC socket
(hearth-core discord.rs while a game runs; `join` here when Discord starts Hearth for a friend's invite).

Which Discord (the owner picks it once, in the bar's chooser or Settings › Discord; saved only on his pick):
  official   the Discord app: Flathub's com.discordapp.Discord (installed when he presses Install) or a .deb's `discord`
  web        Discord's own web app (https://discord.com/app) in a small Hearth Browser (Firefox) window with its own
             profile, nothing to install; he signs in on Discord's own page
  dorion     Dorion (github.com/SpikeHD/Dorion), a lighter unofficial app that loads Discord's web app. Its official
             GitHub release, checked against the SHA-256 GitHub publishes for it, unpacked into ~/.local/opt/dorion

  hearth-discord status                    JSON: client, chosen, clients{official,web,dorion: installed}, running,
                                           appId, enabled, askToJoin, invite (while a game runs), size
  hearth-discord choose CLIENT             save his pick (official | web | dorion)
  hearth-discord set KEY VALUE             enabled / askToJoin (on|off), appId (digits, or "" to take it out)
  hearth-discord install CLIENT            install it (progress lines, then JSON); web needs nothing
  hearth-discord open [--full] [--quick EDGE SCREEN BAR ANCHOR]
                                           start the picked Discord (or the next one there), full size or as the
                                           small window by the bar, placed once its window is up
  hearth-discord place EDGE SCREEN BAR ANCHOR
                                           move and size the open Discord window by the bar (SCREEN is WxH+X+Y, BAR
                                           the bar's thickness, ANCHOR the button's position along the bar or -1)
  hearth-discord geometry EDGE SCREEN BAR ANCHOR   JSON {x, y, w, h}: where `place` puts it
  hearth-discord remember                  keep the open window's size for next time (state, not a setting)
  hearth-discord invite                    JSON: the invite for what you're playing (link, PIN), or null
  hearth-discord join --stdin | --wait [URL] | --link hearth://join/...
                                           a friend's invite: find the game (Play / Install) or start Play together
  hearth-discord notify-bridge --while SOCKET
                                           Steam Game Mode has no notification server: this one takes desktop
                                           notifications (Discord's among them) only when nobody else does, and prints
                                           one JSON line each ({id, app, title, body}) for the Hearth Link plugin to
                                           show as a toast. It gives the name up to anyone who asks for it, and quits
                                           within 3 seconds once SOCKET (Hearth's core in Steam Game Mode) stops
                                           answering, so Desktop Mode's own notifications always get it back.
                                           Nothing is logged or kept
Failures print "error: ..." and exit 1.
"""
